\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Seagulls
\f1\b0 \
CDL Thumb Drive Automation for MacOS\
\

\f0\b What Seagulls Does
\f1\b0 \
Seagulls automates the tedious work of copying your CDLs and framegrabs to a thumb drive for your loader, as well as archiving your framegrabs to an organized folder.\
\

\f0\b Setup:
\f1\b0 \
The first time Seagulls opens, you will be prompted to set up a few folders.  The \'93CDL Folder\'94 should be a working folder to which you export CDLs and framegrabs from Livegrade.  The \'93Framegrab Archive\'94 folder is just that: a folder where you would like to keep your framegrabs.\
\
After setup, Seagulls scans for mounted external drives.  Only \'93removable\'94 drives (thumb drives, as opposed to external hard drives) are shown. Your internal system disk will not appear.\
\
Seagulls assumes you will use a rotation of thumb drives regularly.  Thumb drives that Seagulls has not used are called \'93untrusted\'94 drives.  If you would like to use a new drive, simply click \'93Trust\'94.  This drive will be remembered in the future and automatically chosen when mounted.\
\

\f0\b What Seagulls Does:
\f1\b0 \
When you\'92re ready, click Start Workflow.  Seagulls will prompt you for the shoot day number and the \'93name\'94 of your film break. (In my use case, I call them \'93AM\'94, \'93PM\'94, or \'93All Day\'94.  You can use these from the dropdown menu or type your own.)\
\
Seagulls will then:\
